Polar Native SDK is an unofficial C++20 port based on Polar BLE SDK.
Original software copyright Polar Electro Oy and other original contributors.
Upstream: https://github.com/polarofficial/polar-ble-sdk
Reviewed source: b58e64dcd13d377447d125c16d7cd25ec928bd50
Prior C# comparison revision: f73aca50dafabf7f3dcfe8bb867083922c9c447a (Git history only).
Modifications: C++ protocol/service implementation, Windows C++/WinRT transport,
ABI v2, native diagnostics/replay/GUI, Unity bindings and tests.
Original license: LICENSES/Polar_SDK_License.txt
Original binary test vectors and .proto definitions retain their upstream provenance.
Legacy csharp_namespace schema annotations are inert metadata; no C# SDK is built.
No affiliation, endorsement or official Windows support by Polar is implied.

Statically linked libraries: Protobuf 29.3, Abseil 20240722.0, utf8_range (Protobuf 29.3),
zlib 1.3.1, minizip-ng 4.0.10. GUI only: Dear ImGui 1.91.9b.
Their licenses are included in LICENSES. C++/WinRT headers come from Windows SDK.
The SDK and native GUI have no .NET runtime dependency. Unity supplies its own runtime.

The capability metadata is copied from upstream/documentation/products/polar_device_capabilities.json
at the reviewed upstream commit and embedded into the native library at build time.
